  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1230 PM CDT Sun Sep 20 2026\n\nCloudy and cool conditions today with occasional showers more\nlikely over northeast Nebraska into west-central Iowa. An\nupper-level trough moving through is triggering these showers\nwith moisture pooling on the north side of a stationary boundary\nstretching from southeast KS to western NY. \n\nCool and cloudy conditions will persist through Monday into at\nleast the first half of Tuesday when we start to see a ridge\nbuild back up over the Central Plains. We may not see any\nsignificant breaks in cloud cover until Wednesday though as we \ndon't see the wind reversal back to southerly until Tuesday \nnight. A few showers will be possible overnight Tuesday night \ninto Wednesday as the 850-mb warm front moves through. \n\nWhile southerly flow will help bring in slightly warmer\ntemperatures, we do see the LLJ return advecting in mid-level\nmoisture keeping us from clearing out completely. This will\ntemper the warming trend through the week, with highs starting\nin the low 60s Monday, mid 60s Tuesday through Thursday, and\nupper 60s to low 70s Friday and Saturday. The return of the LLJ\nwill also bring back shower and storm chances Thursday into the\nweekend. Not seeing any signals for any periods of potential\nsevere weather at this time.",
